// sunder's (pinchr's) detector, fitted to the Softube model's gain reduction through time (tone bursts of 2 ms to 1 s at two
// levels and six Attack / Release settings, steps at every Attack and Release position, kick-like bursts), its
// response to frequency, and its sidechain filters. Generated by germcal/export_det5.py (fit_det6): do not edit by hand.
//
//   sidechain -> two first-order high-passes (kHp1Hz, kHp2Hz) -> [SC Filter: a first-order shelf]
//             -> a rectifier (the positive half; the negative half times kNegative)
//             -> a compression w = ((1 + r / kR0)^kGamma - 1) / kGamma (the knee's diodes ahead of the capacitor:
//                short loud bursts charge it little, release slows from deep gain reduction)
//             -> a peak follower (charging with the Attack's time, discharging with the Release's), a one-pole
//                smoother (kSmoothSec) -> the level u (dB) the gain-reduction table reads, through kCalW
